```cpp
#include <cstdint>
#include <stdexcept>

// Invariant: balance_cents_ >= 0.
class BankAccount {
public:
    void deposit(std::int64_t cents) {
        if (cents <= 0) throw std::invalid_argument("deposit must be positive");
        balance_cents_ += cents;
    }
    bool withdraw(std::int64_t cents) {       // false: refused, state unchanged.
        if (cents <= 0 || cents > balance_cents_) return false;
        balance_cents_ -= cents;
        return true;
    }
    std::int64_t balance() const { return balance_cents_; }   // read-only view.
private:
    std::int64_t balance_cents_ = 0;          // money in integer cents.
};
```

| Design choice | Why |
|---|---|
| private data. | only the class can change it. |
| deposit and withdraw, not set_balance. | each operation checks the rule. |
| const balance(). | callers can read without changing. |
| integer cents. | no floating-point rounding drift. |

